                    "patching_rect": [ 751.0, 818.0, 288.0, 194.0 ],
                    "prompt_sent": 0,
                    "prompt_text": "A piece for flute made of 2 interleaved chromatic scales. Structure the line of the flute as two interleaved chromatic lines starting from low D going up. The two lines are identical, but the first one is played in twelfth-harmonics so that the lowest D will be a high A, then D# will be A# and so on. The interleaving idea is that an increasing number of notes of the second line are little by little inserted in between the notes of the first line: first, 0 notes are inserted between the first and second note of the first line; then 1 note of the second line is inserted between the second and third note of the first line; then 2 notes, then 3, 4, 5, etc. I can control starting pitch, offset interval and number of total notes"
                }
            },
